function home(){main.classList.remove('skyLayout');let wave=art('wave',true);main.innerHTML=`<section class="hero"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / LIGHT LABORATORY</span><h1>Look<br>beyond<br><em>the visible.</em></h1><p>From electromagnetic waves to individual photons. Explore the light that tells us about matter and the Universe.</p><div class="actions"><a class="primary" href="#experiments">Choose an experiment ↗</a><a class="textlink" href="#basics">Understand the ideas first</a></div></div><div class="heroart">${wave}</div></section>

<section class="intro" id="basics"><div class="introhead"><div><span class="eyebrow">FIRST, A LITTLE THEORY</span><h2>What is light?</h2></div><p>Light lets us see the world. Its own nature turns out to be more complex than our eyes can reveal.</p></div><div class="theorygrid"><article class="theorycard"><svg class="mini" viewBox="0 0 400 150" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0 75H400" stroke="#EAD8D1"/><path d="M0 75Q25-15 50 75T100 75T150 75T200 75T250 75T300 75T350 75T400 75" fill="none" stroke="#FF4E29" stroke-width="2.5"/><path d="M0 75Q25 145 50 75T100 75T150 75T200 75T250 75T300 75T350 75T400 75" fill="none" stroke="#689b9b" stroke-width="1.5"/><text x="315" y="25" fill="#FF4E29" font-size="13">E ⟂ B</text></svg><span class="eyebrow">01 / WAVE</span><h3>Fields oscillate.</h3><p>An electric charge can act on another charge at a distance. We describe this interaction with an electric field; moving charges also produce a magnetic field. In light, these two fields change together, and the changes travel through space carrying energy. This travelling disturbance is an electromagnetic wave. Light can also travel through empty space: a vacuum.</p><div class="formula"><span role="math" aria-label="lambda equals c divided by nu">λ = <span class="mathfrac" aria-hidden="true"><span>c</span><span>ν</span></span></span></div><p>The distance over which the wave pattern repeats is its wavelength λ. The number of complete oscillations per second is its frequency ν, measured in hertz (Hz). Divide the speed of light c by the frequency to find the wavelength. In a vacuum, c ≈ 3 × 10<sup>8</sup> m/s. The curve shows how the field changes; light does not travel along this curve.</p><a class="textlink" href="#lab/wave">Explore the fields ↗</a></article>
<article class="theorycard"><svg class="mini" viewBox="0 0 400 150" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 75H380" stroke="#EAD8D1" stroke-dasharray="4 7"/><circle cx="70" cy="75" r="9" fill="#FFB19D"/><circle cx="190" cy="75" r="9" fill="#FF8F73"/><circle cx="310" cy="75" r="9" fill="#FF4E29"/><text x="55" y="120" fill="#FF4E29" font-size="12">event</text><text x="171" y="120" fill="#FF4E29" font-size="12">event</text><text x="290" y="120" fill="#FF4E29" font-size="12">event</text></svg><span class="eyebrow">02 / PHOTON</span><h3>Energy is transferred in quanta.</h3><p>A detector receives light energy in discrete packets. Each packet is a quantum of light, or photon. Its energy E depends on frequency: a blue photon carries more energy than a red photon. Planck\u0027s constant h connects frequency and energy: h = 6.62607015 × 10<sup>−34</sup> J·s.</p><div class="formula">E = hν = hc/λ</div><p>A larger photon flux means more events per second. Each photon\u0027s energy is determined by its frequency. The circles represent detections, not the shape of photons.</p><a class="textlink" href="#lab/photoelectric">Test the photoelectric effect ↗</a></article>
<article class="theorycard wide"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / TWO ASPECTS OF LIGHT</span><h2>Individual detections.<br>A wave-like pattern.</h2><p>Photons are detected one at a time, yet many detections in a double-slit experiment build up interference fringes. Bright fringes are places with more detections; dark fringes are places where detections are unlikely. This combination of discrete energy transfers and wave-like patterns is called wave–particle duality.</p><a class="primary" href="#lab/interference">Try the double-slit experiment ↗</a></div><div><div class="formula">P(x) ∝ |ψ(x)|²</div><p>P(x) describes the probability density of a detection near position x; ψ is the mathematical quantity used to calculate this probability, the probability amplitude. Vertical bars mean the magnitude. The symbol ∝ means “proportional to”: after normalisation, the probability over the entire screen is 1. Two contributions with a stable phase relationship can reinforce or cancel each other. These contributions are called coherent.</p></div></article>
<article class="theorycard"><span class="eyebrow">04 / MORE THAN A RAINBOW</span><h3>One electromagnetic spectrum.</h3><p>Radio waves, microwaves, infrared, visible, ultraviolet, X-rays and gamma rays are electromagnetic radiation at different frequencies.</p><div class="spectrum"></div><div class="spectrumlabels"><span>380 nm · violet</span><span>780 nm · red</span></div><p style="margin-top:18px">The limits of visible light are approximate and depend on the eye\u0027s sensitivity. Colour results from the interaction between a spectrum and our visual system.</p></article><article class="theorycard"><span class="eyebrow">05 / INFORMATION IN LIGHT</span><h3>A spectrum reveals its source.</h3><p>Atoms and molecules absorb and emit light at characteristic transitions. Hot objects have broad thermal spectra. An atmosphere changes light by scattering and absorption.</p><p>This is how we study gas composition, stellar temperatures and planetary atmospheres. Each experiment explores one part of that story.</p><a class="textlink" href="#lab/atom">From atoms to spectra ↗</a></article></div></section>
<section class="catalog" id="experiments"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR TURN TO EXPLORE</span><h2>Where shall we start?</h2><p class="muted">Choose a topic. Change one parameter, record the result and try to explain what you see.</p><div class="groupbar" role="group" aria-label="Experiment groups"><button class="active" data-group="all">All experiments</button>${groups.map((g,i)=>`<button data-group="${i}">${g}</button>`).join('')}</div><div class="cards">${exps.map((e,i)=>`<a class="expcard" data-category="${e.group}" href="#lab/${e.id}"><div class="cardart">${art(e.id)}</div><div class="cardbody"><small>${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / ${groups[e.group]}</small><h3>${e.title}</h3><p>${e.short}</p><span class="go">Open experiment <span>↗</span></span></div></a>`).join('')}</div></section><section class="sourceshome"><strong>What the models are based on</strong><p>Optics and quantum physics — <a href="https://openstax.org/details/books/university-physics-volume-3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStax, University Physics, Volume 3 ↗</a>. Sky colour — <a href="https://www.weather.gov/fgz/SkyBlue" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Weather Service ↗</a>. Colour-matching functions — <a href="https://jcgt.org/published/0002/02/01/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wyman, Sloan & Shirley (2013) ↗</a>. The equations, approximations and sources for each experiment are listed below it.</p><p class="safety">These digital experiments require no lasers or UV sources. In physical experiments, never point a laser at anyone\u0027s eyes or look at the Sun without appropriate protection.</p></section>`;
$('.groupbar').addEventListener('click',ev=>{let b=ev.target.closest('button');if(!b)return;document.querySelectorAll('[data-group]').forEach(x=>x.classList.toggle('active',x===b));document.querySelectorAll('.expcard').forEach(x=>x.hidden=b.dataset.group!=='all'&&x.dataset.category!==b.dataset.group)});}
function modeTabs(e){let options=e.id==='interference'?[['photons','Individual detections'],['wave','Wave prediction']]:e.id==='refraction'?[['0','Refraction'],['1','Dispersion: prism']]:e.id==='polarization'?[['lab','Wave and filters'],['water','Glare from water']]:null;return options?`<div class="modebar" role="group" aria-label="Experiment mode">${options.map(([v,l])=>`<button data-mode="${v}">${l}</button>`).join('')}</div>`:''}
function mathMarkup(s){return String(s).replaceAll('I/Iref','I/I<sub>ref</sub>').replaceAll('I/I₀','I/I<sub>ref</sub>').replaceAll('E₀,ref','E<sub>0,ref</sub>').replaceAll('Kmax','K<sub>max</sub>').replaceAll('λmax','λ<sub>max</sub>').replaceAll('τR','τ<sub>R</sub>').replaceAll('fgas','f<sub>gas</sub>').replaceAll('Ustop','U<sub>stop</sub>').replaceAll('λabs','λ<sub>abs</sub>').replaceAll('λem','λ<sub>em</sub>').replaceAll('Iin','I<sub>in</sub>').replaceAll('Iout','I<sub>out</sub>').replaceAll('θcrit','θ<sub>crit</sub>').replaceAll('Bλ','B<sub>λ</sub>').replaceAll('R☉','R<sub>☉</sub>').replaceAll('L☉','L<sub>☉</sub>')}
function fieldHTML(f){if(f.options)return `<div class="field"><label for="p-${f.key}"><span>${mathMarkup(f.label)}</span></label><select id="p-${f.key}" data-param="${f.key}">${f.options.map(([v,l])=>`<option value="${v}" ${String(params[f.key])===v?'selected':''}>${l}</option>`).join('')}</select>${f.key==='planet'?'<p id="skyGravity"></p>':''}</div>`;return `<div class="field"><label for="p-${f.key}"><span>${mathMarkup(f.label)}</span><output id="o-${f.key}">${number(params[f.key])} ${mathMarkup(f.unit)}</output></label><input data-param="${f.key}" id="p-${f.key}" type="range" min="${f.min}" max="${f.max}" step="${f.step}" value="${params[f.key]}"><div class="rangeends"><span>${f.min} ${mathMarkup(f.unit)}</span><span>${f.max} ${mathMarkup(f.unit)}</span></div></div>`}
let skyTimer;function lab(e){main.classList.toggle('skyLayout',e.id==='sky');clearInterval(skyTimer);active=e;params=defaults(e);let saved;try{saved=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem('light-params-'+e.id)||'null')}catch{}if(saved)for(let f of e.fields){let v=saved[f.key];if(f.options&&f.options.some(q=>q[0]===String(v)))params[f.key]=isNaN(Number(v))?v:Number(v);else if(!f.options&&Number.isFinite(v))params[f.key]=P.clamp(v,f.min,f.max)}if(e.id==='sky'){const preset=fixedAtmosphere(params.planet);if(saved)for(const k of ['dust','dustH','radius','aerosol','angstrom','asymmetry','albedo','ozone','ground','displayMode','exposure'])if(saved[k]!==undefined)delete preset[k];Object.assign(params,preset,dayPosition(params.dayPhase,params.latitude));if(saved?.transportVersion!==2&&params.planet==='mars')params.radius=1.4;params.transportVersion=2;params.skyView='panorama';normaliseMix(params);}if(e.id==='atom')params.lower=Math.min(params.lower,params.upper-1);time=0;photons=[];running=false;let i=exps.indexOf(e);document.title=e.title+' | Light — INSCIENCE LAB';main.innerHTML=`<section class="exphead"><a class="back" href="#experiments">← Back to experiments</a><span class="eyebrow" style="margin:20px 0 0">${String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')} / ${groups[e.group]}</span><h1>${e.title}</h1><p>${e.sub}</p></section><div class="labgrid"><div><section class="stage">${modeTabs(e)}<div class="stagebar"><span>CHANGE A PARAMETER → OBSERVE THE RESULT</span><span id="status">Ready to start</span></div>${e.id==='atom'?'<div id="atomIdentity" class="atomicIdentity"></div>':''}${e.id==='refraction'?`<div class="sceneTools" id="prismTools" hidden>${e.fields.filter(f=>['prismView','prismZoom'].includes(f.key)).map(fieldHTML).join('')}<button id="prismHome" type="button">↺ Whole prism</button><p>Drag with a mouse or finger. Use the arrow keys to pan.</p></div>`:''}${e.id==='interference'?'<div class="photonTools" id="photonTools"><button type="button" data-add-photons="1">+1 detection</button><button type="button" data-add-photons="100">+100</button><button type="button" data-add-photons="1000">+1000</button><span>Each new detection is added to the previous ones.</span></div>':''}${e.id==='polarization'?'<div class="sceneTools" id="waterBeamTools" hidden></div>':''}${e.id==='sky'?'<div class="sceneTools skyTools"><button id="skyRise">▶ Sunrise / sunset</button><button id="skySunset" type="button">Martian sunset</button><button id="skyRandom" hidden>↻ Random atmosphere</button><span id="skyMotionNote">Daytime arc: sunrise → noon → sunset.</span></div>':''}${e.id==='sky'?'<div class="sceneTools">'+e.fields.filter(f=>f.key==='skyView').map(fieldHTML).join('')+'</div>':''}${e.id==='sky'?`<div class="skyViewportGrid"><figure><figcaption>Whole sky</figcaption><canvas id="scene" role="img" aria-label="Sky panorama: interactive visualisation"></canvas></figure><figure><figcaption>Sky around the Sun</figcaption><canvas id="sunScene" role="img" aria-label="Close-up sky view: camera points at the Sun"></canvas><div class="solarCameraControl">${e.fields.filter(f=>f.key==='sunFov').map(fieldHTML).join('')}</div></figure></div><p class="skyViewNote">Both views use the same calculation and exposure. The camera on the right points at the Sun; the dark area below the horizon is the surface. Tap the sky to select a direction for the spectrum.</p><a class="skyTheoryLink" href="#calculations">How does this colour arise? Explanation ↓</a>`:`<canvas id="scene" role="img" aria-label="${e.title}: interactive visualisation"></canvas>`}<div class="live" id="live"></div>${e.id==='polarization'?'<div id="waterCompare" class="waterCompare" hidden></div>':''}<div class="transport"><button class="primary" id="play">▶ Start experiment</button><button id="reset">↺ Reset</button><button id="step">Step 0.1 s</button><button id="record">＋ Record measurement</button></div><p class="stagefoot" id="time">Animation time: 0 s</p><p class="stagefoot">${mathMarkup(e.note)}</p></section><section class="chartbox"><h3 id="curveTitle">${e.id==='interference'?'Theoretical distribution · not accumulated detections':e.id==='sky'?'Spectra: orange — sky, ochre — direct light':'Experiment graph'}</h3>${e.id==='sky'?e.fields.filter(f=>f.key==='skyPlot').map(fieldHTML).join(''):''}<canvas id="curve" aria-label="${e.axis.join('; ')}"></canvas><p class="chartRead" id="read">Hover over or touch the graph to read a value.</p></section><section class="calculated"><span class="eyebrow">CALCULATION FOR YOUR PARAMETERS</span><div id="worked"></div></section></div><aside class="settings"><h3>Experiment settings</h3><p>${animatedIds.includes(e.id)?'Changing a parameter resets the time and accumulated events.':'Changing a parameter updates the diagram and calculation immediately.'} Notebook records are preserved.</p>${e.fields.filter(f=>!(e.id==='refraction'&&['prismView','prismZoom'].includes(f.key))&&!(e.id==='sky'&&['skyView','skyPlot','sunFov'].includes(f.key))).map(fieldHTML).join('')}${e.id==='sky'?'<p id="gasMix"></p>':''}<div class="note"><strong>What to look for</strong><p>${mathMarkup(e.observe)}</p><a class="textlink" href="#calculations">Theory and calculations ↓</a></div></aside></div><div class="under" id="calculations"><article class="theoryarticle"><span class="eyebrow">FROM OBSERVATION TO EXPLANATION</span><h2>What are we seeing?</h2>${e.theory.map(([h,p])=>`<section><h3>${h}</h3><div>${p}</div></section>`).join('')}<div class="sources"><strong>Sources</strong><p><a href="${e.source}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${e.id==='sky'?'National Weather Service':'OpenStax: textbook'} ↗</a>${e.id==='polarization'?'<a href="https://www.rp-photonics.com/fresnel_equations.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Fresnel equations: RP Photonics ↗</a>':''}${['sky','blackbody'].includes(e.id)?'<a href="https://jcgt.org/published/0002/02/01/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Approximation of colour-matching functions ↗</a>':''}</p></div></article><aside class="theoryaside"><div class="task"><span class="eyebrow">TRY IT YOURSELF</span><h3>Mini laboratory</h3><p>${mathMarkup(e.task)}</p><button id="preset">Set initial parameters ↗</button></div><div class="task" style="background:white;border:1px solid var(--line)"><h3>How to record a result</h3><ol><li>Set the parameters.</li><li>${animatedIds.includes(e.id)?'Start the experiment or keep the static state.':'Wait for the diagram to update.'}</li><li>Click “Record measurement”.</li><li>Change one parameter and repeat.</li><li>Open the notebook, choose graph axes and save the CSV.</li></ol></div><div class="callout"><strong>Model limits</strong><p>${mathMarkup(e.limit)}</p></div><div class="actions">${i?`<a class="textlink" href="#lab/${exps[i-1].id}">← Previous</a>`:''}${i<exps.length-1?`<a class="textlink" href="#lab/${exps[i+1].id}">Next →</a>`:''}</div></aside></div>`;
if(e.id==='sky')$('#skySunset').onclick=()=>$('#preset').click();
if(e.id==='sky'){document.querySelectorAll('a[href="#calculations"]').forEach(link=>link.addEventListener('click',ev=>{ev.preventDefault();$('#calculations').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})}));const article=$('#calculations'),tasks=article.querySelector('.theoryaside');$('.labgrid > div').append(article);$('.settings').append(tasks);$('#sunScene').addEventListener('pointerdown',ev=>{const b=ev.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect(),ray=sunCameraRay(params,(ev.clientX-b.left)/b.width,(ev.clientY-b.top)/b.height,Number(params.sunFov||20),b.width/b.height);if(ray.elevation<0)return;params.view=Math.round(ray.elevation);params.azimuth=Math.round(((ray.azimuth-(params.sunAz||0)+540)%360)-180);for(const k of ['view','azimuth']){$('#p-'+k).value=params[k];$('#o-'+k).textContent=params[k]+' °'}render()});}
if(e.id==='sky')$('#skyRandom').onclick=()=>{params.planet='custom';const rand=(a,b)=>a+Math.random()*(b-a);Object.assign(params,{oxygen:rand(0,35),co2:rand(0,90),hydrogen:rand(0,80),logP:rand(2,5.2),airT:Math.round(rand(170,330)),dust:Math.round(rand(0,.4)*100)/100,radius:[.5,1.6,3][Math.floor(Math.random()*3)],dustH:Math.round(rand(3,15)),planetRadius:Math.round(rand(3000,12000)/100)*100,gravity:Math.round(rand(3,20)*10)/10});normaliseMix(params);for(const f of e.fields){$('#p-'+f.key).value=params[f.key];if($('#o-'+f.key))$('#o-'+f.key).textContent=number(params[f.key])+' '+(f.unit||'')}reset();};if(e.id==='sky')$('#scene').addEventListener('pointerdown',ev=>{const b=ev.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect();const width=200,center=0,maxElev=90;params.azimuth=Math.round(P.clamp((ev.clientX-b.left)/b.width*width+center-width/2-(params.sunAz||0),-180,180));params.view=Math.round(P.clamp((b.height-56-(ev.clientY-b.top))/(b.height-104)*maxElev,0,90));for(const k of ['azimuth','view']){$('#p-'+k).value=params[k];$('#o-'+k).textContent=params[k]+' °'}render()});if(e.id==='sky')$('#skyRise').onclick=()=>{if(skyTimer){clearInterval(skyTimer);skyTimer=null;$('#skyRise').textContent='▶ Sunrise / sunset';return}if(params.dayPhase>=180)params.dayPhase=0;$('#skyRise').textContent='Ⅱ Pause';skyTimer=setInterval(()=>{if($('#record').disabled)return;params.dayPhase=Math.min(180,params.dayPhase+3);Object.assign(params,dayPosition(params.dayPhase,params.latitude));$('#p-dayPhase').value=params.dayPhase;$('#o-dayPhase').textContent=params.dayPhase+' °';$('#p-sun').value=params.sun;$('#o-sun').textContent=number(params.sun)+' °';render();if(params.dayPhase===180){clearInterval(skyTimer);skyTimer=null;$('#skyRise').textContent='▶ Repeat the daytime path'}},500)};if(e.id==='refraction')bindPrismViewport();if(e.id==='interference')document.querySelectorAll('[data-add-photons]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{running=false;cancelAnimationFrame(frame);time=Math.min(12000,photons.length+Number(b.dataset.addPhotons))/params.rate;updatePhotons();updateButtons();render();});document.querySelectorAll('[data-mode]').forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>{let key=e.id==='refraction'?'prism':'mode';params[key]=e.id==='refraction'?Number(b.dataset.mode):b.dataset.mode;$('#p-'+key).value=params[key];try{sessionStorage.setItem('light-params-'+e.id,JSON.stringify(params))}catch{}reset()});$('#play').onclick=()=>{if(Number.isFinite(transitionDuration())&&time>=transitionDuration()){time=0;if(active.id==='interference')photons=[];}running=!running;cancelAnimationFrame(frame);last=performance.now();updateButtons();if(running)frame=requestAnimationFrame(tick)};$('#reset').onclick=()=>reset();$('#step').onclick=()=>{running=false;time=Math.min(transitionDuration(),time+.1);updatePhotons();syncControls();updateButtons();render()};$('#record').onclick=record;$('#preset').onclick=()=>{params={...params,...e.preset};if(e.id==='sky'){Object.assign(params,dayPosition(params.dayPhase,params.latitude));try{sessionStorage.setItem('light-params-sky',JSON.stringify(params))}catch{}}for(let f of e.fields){$('#p-'+f.key).value=params[f.key];if(!f.options)$('#o-'+f.key).innerHTML=number(params[f.key])+' '+mathMarkup(f.unit)}reset();scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})};document.querySelectorAll('[data-param]').forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('input',()=>{let f=e.fields.find(q=>q.key===el.dataset.param),v=el.value;if(e.id==='interference'&&f.key==='prediction'){params.prediction=Number(v);render();return;}if(f.key==='planet'){let vals=fixedAtmosphere(v);Object.assign(params,vals);for(const [k,n]of Object.entries(vals)){$('#p-'+k).value=n;if($('#o-'+k))$('#o-'+k).textContent=number(n)+' '+(e.fields.find(f=>f.key===k).unit||'')}}if(f.key==='species'){params.atomicLine=P.atomicSpecies[v]?.lines[0]?.[0]||'first';}if(f.key==='prismView'){params.panX=0;params.panY=0;}params[f.key]=f.options?(isNaN(Number(v))?v:Number(v)):Number(v);if(e.id==='sky'&&['oxygen','co2','hydrogen'].includes(f.key)){normaliseMix(params,f.key);for(const k of ['oxygen','co2','hydrogen']){$('#p-'+k).value=params[k];$('#o-'+k).textContent=number(params[k])+' %'}}if(e.id==='sky'&&['dayPhase','latitude'].includes(f.key))Object.assign(params,dayPosition(params.dayPhase,params.latitude));if(e.id==='atom'&&params.lower>=params.upper){params.lower=params.upper-1;$('#p-lower').value=params.lower;$('#o-lower').textContent=number(params.lower)}if(!f.options)$('#o-'+f.key).innerHTML=number(params[f.key])+' '+mathMarkup(f.unit);try{sessionStorage.setItem('light-params-'+e.id,JSON.stringify(params))}catch{}reset()}));$('#curve').addEventListener('pointermove',ev=>{if(!drawCache)return;let b=ev.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect(),q=drawChart($('#curve'),drawCache,ev.clientX-b.left);if(q)$('#read').textContent=`${drawCache.xlabel}: ${fmt(q[0])} · ${drawCache.ylabel}: ${fmt(q[1])}`});$('#curve').addEventListener('pointerleave',()=>{if(drawCache)drawChart($('#curve'),drawCache)});buildCDF();syncControls();updateButtons();render();}
function transitionDuration(){return active?.id==='interference'&&params.mode==='photons'?12000/params.rate:active?.id==='atom'?5:active?.id==='molecule'?(params.view==='levels'?6:7):Infinity}
const animatedIds=['wave','interference','photoelectric','atom','molecule','polarization'];
function syncControls(){let staticExp=!animatedIds.includes(active.id);$('#scene').classList.toggle('interferenceScene',active.id==='interference');$('#scene').classList.toggle('polarizationScene',active.id==='polarization');if(active.id==='interference')$('#photonTools').hidden=params.mode!=='photons';['#play','#step','#time'].forEach(s=>$(s).hidden=staticExp);let disable={};if(active.id==='interference')disable={rate:params.mode!=='photons',prediction:params.mode!=='photons'};if(active.id==='sky')disable=Object.fromEntries(active.fields.map(f=>[f.key,f.key==='mode'||(f.key==='marsTime'?params.mode!=='mars':params.mode==='mars')]));if(active.id==='diffraction')disable={spacing:params.kind!=='grating',n:params.kind!=='grating'};if(active.id==='polarization')disable={middle:params.count!==3,angle:params.count===1,input:params.mode==='water',inputAngle:params.mode==='water'||!['linear','elliptical'].includes(params.input),ellipticity:params.mode==='water'||params.input!=='elliptical',incidence:params.mode!=='water',waterBeam:true,waterExposure:params.mode!=='water'};if(active.id==='refraction')disable={lambda:!!params.prism,angle:!!params.prism,reverse:!!params.prism,prismAngle:!params.prism,apex:!params.prism,prismView:!params.prism,prismZoom:!params.prism};$('#scene').classList.toggle('molecularLevels',active.id==='molecule'&&params.view==='levels');if(active.id==='molecule')disable={v:params.transition!=='electronic',J:params.transition==='fluorescence'};for(let f of active.fields){$('#p-'+f.key).disabled=!!disable[f.key];let hide=(active.id==='sky'&&!!disable[f.key])||(active.id==='interference'&&(f.key==='mode'||!!disable[f.key]))||(active.id==='refraction'&&(f.key==='prism'||(params.prism&&['lambda','angle','reverse'].includes(f.key))||(!params.prism&&['prismAngle','apex','prismView','prismZoom'].includes(f.key))))||(active.id==='polarization'&&(f.key==='mode'||!!disable[f.key]));$('#p-'+f.key).closest('.field').hidden=hide}document.querySelectorAll('[data-mode]').forEach(b=>{let chosen=String(params[active.id==='refraction'?'prism':'mode'])===b.dataset.mode;b.classList.toggle('active',chosen);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(chosen))});if(active.id==='refraction'){$('label[for="p-material"]').textContent=params.prism?'Prism material':'Second medium';$('#prismTools').hidden=!params.prism;$('#scene').classList.toggle('pannable',!!params.prism);$('#scene').tabIndex=params.prism?0:-1;}if(active.id==='atom'){const species=params.species||'H',g=P.atomicGround[species],q=P.atom(params);$('#atomIdentity').innerHTML=`<strong>${P.atomicSpecies[species].name}: ${g.electrons} ${g.electrons===1?'electron':[2,3,4].includes(g.electrons)?'electrons':'electrons'} in the neutral atom</strong><br>Ground configuration: ${g.configuration}.<br>${species==='H'?'Ground state: n = 1. The marks n = 1…10 are possible energies of one electron, not ten occupied shells.':'Two selected states of the whole atom are shown, not the filling of its electron shells. [He], [Ne] and [Ar] denote filled inner shells of the corresponding noble gas.'}<br>${params.kind==='emission'?'The atom is initially prepared in an excited state.':'The atom is initially prepared in the lower state of the selected transition.'}`;const tab=params.species!=='H'&&!!params.species;for(const key of ['upper','lower'])$('#p-'+key).closest('.field').hidden=tab;$('#p-atomicLine').closest('.field').hidden=!tab;$('.settings .note p').textContent=tab?'Selected neutral atom: '+P.atomicSpecies[params.species].name+'. Choose a tabulated transition and run one process. Compare the photon colour, vacuum wavelength and energy. State labels and the NIST source appear in the calculation. Colours for UV and infrared are illustrative.':active.observe;if(tab){const a=P.atomicSpecies[params.species];const control=$('#p-atomicLine');control.innerHTML=a.lines.map(l=>`<option value="${l[0]}">${l[1].toLocaleString('en-GB')} nm (${l[1]<200?'vacuum':'air'}) · ${params.kind==='emission'?l[5]+' → '+l[4]:l[4]+' → '+l[5]}</option>`).join('');control.value=a.lines.some(l=>l[0]===params.atomicLine)?params.atomicLine:a.lines[0][0];}$('#p-lower').max=params.upper-1;$('#p-lower').closest('.field').querySelector('.rangeends span:last-child').textContent=params.upper-1;}if(active.id==='interference')$('#step').hidden=true;if(active.id==='sky'){$('#p-skyView').closest('.field').hidden=true;$('#skyMotionNote').textContent='The panorama stays fixed. The camera on the right tracks the Sun.';const custom=params.planet==='custom';$('#skyGravity').hidden=custom;$('#skyGravity').textContent='Acceleration due to gravity g = '+number(params.planet==='mars'?3.71:9.81)+' m/s² · fixed';$('#p-sun').closest('.field').hidden=true;for(const key of ['logP','airT','oxygen','co2','hydrogen','planetRadius','gravity'])$('#p-'+key).closest('.field').hidden=!custom;$('#p-radius').closest('.field').hidden=params.aerosol==='haze';for(const k of ['angstrom','asymmetry','albedo'])$('#p-'+k).closest('.field').hidden=params.aerosol!=='haze';$('#skyRandom').hidden=!custom;$('#gasMix').textContent='Composition: N₂ '+number(Math.max(0,100-params.oxygen-params.co2-params.hydrogen)<1e-8?0:100-params.oxygen-params.co2-params.hydrogen)+'% · O₂ '+number(params.oxygen)+'% · CO₂ '+number(params.co2)+'% · H₂ '+number(params.hydrogen)+'%. Total: 100%.';}if(active.id==='sky'){const mars=params.mode==='mars';$('.settings > p').textContent=mars?'Choose a time of day: the diagram updates immediately. This illustration has no numerical calculation.':'After changing a parameter, wait for the spectral calculation. Notebook records are preserved.';$('#curve').closest('.chartbox').hidden=mars;$('#record').disabled=mars;$('#scene').setAttribute('aria-label',mars?'Mars: explanatory sky-colour diagram':'Atmosphere with gas and dust: interactive panorama');$('.settings .note p').textContent=mars?'Choose daytime or sunset. At sunset, the blue region is shown only near the Sun; the background remains warm. This is a diagram: numerical spectra and measurement recording are disabled for it.':active.observe;$('.calculated .eyebrow').textContent=mars?'DIAGRAM EXPLANATION':'CALCULATION FOR YOUR PARAMETERS';$('.stage > p.stagefoot:last-child').textContent=mars?'Illustration of the observed effect of Martian dust. Colours and sizes are schematic; this diagram does not calculate a spectrum or predict a particular sunset.':active.note;}if(staticExp)$('#status').textContent='Change parameters · immediate result'}
function updateButtons(){if(!active)return;$('#play').textContent=running?'Ⅱ Pause':Number.isFinite(transitionDuration())&&time>=transitionDuration()?(active.id==='interference'?'▶ Start a new accumulation':'▶ Repeat transition'):(active.id==='interference'?(params.mode==='photons'?'▶ Start accumulating':'▶ Start animation'):'▶ Start experiment');$('#step').disabled=running;$('#status').textContent=!animatedIds.includes(active.id)?'The result updates immediately':running?'Experiment running':Number.isFinite(transitionDuration())&&time>=transitionDuration()?(active.id==='interference'?'Accumulation complete':'Transition complete'):time?'Pause':'Ready to start'}
function reset(){clearInterval(skyTimer);skyTimer=null;if(active?.id==='sky'&&$('#skyRise'))$('#skyRise').textContent='▶ Sunrise / sunset';running=false;cancelAnimationFrame(frame);time=0;photons=[];buildCDF();syncControls();updateButtons();render()}
function buildCDF(){cdf=[];if(active?.id!=='interference')return;let extent=.015,sum=0;for(let i=0;i<2000;i++){let x=-extent+2*extent*(i+.5)/2000;sum+=P.fringe(x,params);cdf.push({x,sum})}for(let q of cdf)q.sum/=sum}
function updatePhotons(){if(active?.id!=='interference'||params.mode!=='photons')return;let count=Math.min(12000,Math.floor(time*params.rate+1e-8));while(photons.length<count){let u=Math.random(),lo=0,hi=cdf.length-1;while(lo<hi){let m=(lo+hi)>>1;if(cdf[m].sum<u)lo=m+1;else hi=m}photons.push({x:cdf[lo].x,jitter:Math.random()})}}
function render(animated=false){if(!active||!$('#scene'))return;if(active.id==='sky'&&!requestSky(params,()=>{if(active?.id==='sky')render()},message=>{if($('#status'))$('#status').textContent=englishStatus(message)})){const c=$('#scene'),ctx=c.getContext('2d');ctx.save();ctx.setTransform(1,0,0,1,0,0);ctx.clearRect(0,0,c.width,c.height);ctx.fillStyle='#181513';ctx.fillRect(0,0,c.width,c.height);ctx.fillStyle='white';ctx.font='24px NAMU, sans-serif';ctx.textAlign='center';ctx.fillText('Calculating light in the atmosphere…',c.width/2,c.height/2);ctx.restore();const solar=$('#sunScene'),sc=solar.getContext('2d');sc.save();sc.setTransform(1,0,0,1,0,0);sc.clearRect(0,0,solar.width,solar.height);sc.restore();$('#live').textContent='Calculating the new parameters…';$('#worked').textContent='Waiting for a new result…';const chart=$('#curve');chart.getContext('2d').clearRect(0,0,chart.width,chart.height);drawCache=null;$('#record').disabled=true;return}if(active.id==='sky'){$('#record').disabled=false;$('#status').textContent='Spectral calculation complete'}let isAnim=animatedIds.includes(active.id);if(!animated||isAnim)drawScene($('#scene'),active,params,time,photons);if(active.id==='sky')drawSunCloseup($('#sunScene'),params);if((!animated||active.id==='wave')&&!(active.id==='sky'&&params.mode==='mars')){drawCache=chartData(active,params,time);if(active.id==='sky')$('#curveTitle').textContent=params.skyPlot==='tau'?'How gas scatters different wavelengths':params.skyPlot==='shape'?'Spectral shapes: sky and direct light':'Light spectrum from the selected sky direction';$('#curve').setAttribute('aria-label',drawCache.xlabel+'; '+drawCache.ylabel);drawChart($('#curve'),drawCache)}if(!animated){$('#worked').innerHTML=mathMarkup(worked(active.id,params));if(active.id==='polarization')renderWaterCompare(params);}let out=active.id==='sky'?(()=>{let q=selectedSky(params);return {'Pressure (Pa)':q.q.pressure,'Stellar altitude (deg)':params.sun,'Scattering angle (deg)':q.theta,'Gas scale height (km)':q.q.H,'Acceleration due to gravity (m/s²)':q.q.g,'Mean molecular mass (u)':q.meanMass,'Gas optical depth at 550 nm':q.gasTau550,'Dust optical depth at 550 nm':params.dust,'Integrated sky signal (relative/sr)':q.relative}})():P.outputs(active.id,params,time);$('#live').innerHTML=Object.entries(out).map(([k,v])=>`<span>${mathMarkup(k)}: <b>${active.id==='sky'&&(k.includes('Gas optical depth')||k.includes('Integrated signal'))?fmt(v,6):number(v)}</b></span>`).join('');$('#time').textContent=`Animation time: ${number(time)} s${active.id==='interference'?' · '+photons.length+' detections (maximum 12,000 in the field)':''}`}
function renderWaterCompare(p){let box=$('#waterCompare');box.hidden=p.mode!=='water';$('#waterBeamTools').hidden=box.hidden;if(box.hidden)return;let q=P.polarization(p),light=P.waterLight(p),signal=light.detailBefore,trans=light.detailTransmission;let tools=$('#waterBeamTools');tools.hidden=false;tools.innerHTML=`<strong>Two light components reach the eye</strong><p>Surface glare + light from objects underwater. The 3D diagram below shows only <b>${p.waterBeam==='detail'?'light from the underwater detail':'glare'}</b>. The fish image combines both components. The 3D scale is normalised to the selected input component; absolute intensities are listed below.</p>${active.fields.filter(f=>f.key==='waterBeam').map(f=>fieldHTML({...f,key:'waterBeamScene'})).join('')}`;const beamControl=tools.querySelector('select');beamControl.value=p.waterBeam;beamControl.addEventListener('change',()=>{params.waterBeam=beamControl.value;$('#p-waterBeam').value=params.waterBeam;try{sessionStorage.setItem('light-params-polarization',JSON.stringify(params))}catch{}render()});const view=(name,glare,fish,tag)=>{let g=Math.min(.96,glare/(glare+fish+1e-30)),brightness=(glare+fish)>1e-14?(p.waterExposure==='contrast'?1:Math.min(1,((glare+fish)/(q.glareBefore+signal))**(1/2.2))):0;return `<div><strong>${name}</strong><svg viewBox="0 0 300 150" role="img" aria-label="Schematic comparison of underwater visibility"><rect width="300" height="150" fill="#264b61"/><path d="M0 120Q80 90 160 115T300 105V150H0" fill="#426f76"/><g opacity="${fish>1e-14?1:0}"><ellipse cx="155" cy="92" rx="35" ry="14" fill="#b7cdb0"/><path d="M125 92L100 73V111Z" fill="#b7cdb0"/><circle cx="175" cy="88" r="3" fill="#183741"/><path d="M15 145Q32 95 20 85M50 150Q58 100 77 94M260 150Q245 100 259 85" fill="none" stroke="#82a8a0" stroke-width="5"/></g><g opacity="${g}"><rect width="300" height="150" fill="#d8e5e8"/><path d="M0 40Q40 5 85 40T175 37T300 40M0 90Q55 70 110 90T220 87T300 95" fill="none" stroke="white" stroke-width="17"/></g><rect width="300" height="150" fill="black" opacity="${1-brightness}"/></svg><small>${tag}</small></div>`};box.innerHTML=`<p><strong>Light reaching the eye after the filters:</strong><br>glare ${fmt(100*light.glareAfter,6)} % + underwater detail ${fmt(100*light.detailAfter,4)} % = total ${fmt(100*light.totalAfter,4)} % of the illumination.<br>${light.totalAfter<1e-14?'Both components are extinguished. The image is black.':'Even when glare is almost extinguished, light from the detail can still pass through.'}</p><div class="waterViews">${view('Without a filter',q.glareBefore,signal,`Glare: ${fmt(100*q.glareBefore,4)} % · detail: ${fmt(100*signal,3)} % of illumination`)}${view('Through the selected filters',q.glareAfter,signal*trans,`Glare: ${fmt(100*q.glareAfter,4)} % · detail: ${fmt(100*signal*trans,3)} % of illumination`)}</div><p>The underwater detail is schematic: its light reaching the eye is assumed unpolarised, with an intensity of 0.02 of the illuminating flux. Glare is calculated using Fresnel equations; the detail also dims through the filters. ${p.waterExposure==='contrast'?'The brightness of the two images is normalised separately to compare contrast, not absolute brightness.':'Same illustrative exposure: the filtered image darkens as the total signal decreases.'} Values are percentages of the same illuminating flux. Image rendering is approximate; it is not a calculation of underwater imaging optics. Colours and objects are schematic.</p>`}
function worked(id,p){if(id==='sky'&&p.mode==='simulation'){let q=selectedSky(p);return `P = 10<sup>${fmt(p.logP)}</sup> = ${fmt(q.q.pressure)} Pa<br>H = k<sub>B</sub>T/(m̄g) = ${fmt(q.q.H)} km<br>Scattering angle: ${fmt(q.theta)}°<br>Fractions [N₂, O₂, CO₂, H₂]: ${q.q.f.map(x=>fmt(100*x,1)+'%').join(', ')}<br>τ<sub>dust</sub>(550 nm) = ${p.dust}. Spherical radiative transfer with multiple scattering and surface reflection.<br>Integrated signal = ${fmt(q.relative,6)} ± ${fmt(q.stderr,6)} relative/sr (upper estimate of 1σ for multiple scattering). This does not include optical-data or grid uncertainty.${q.cut?`<br>Warning: ${q.cut} paths reached the scattering-order limit; convergence should be checked.`:""}`}if(id==='sky'&&p.mode==='mars')return p.marsTime==='sunset'?'At sunset, light travels farther through dust. Blue scattered light is concentrated near the Sun\u0027s direction, not across the whole sky. Diagram colours illustrate observations; there is no spectral calculation here.':'During the day, suspended mineral dust often gives the sky a yellowish-rust colour. CO₂ alone does not explain this. The colours are schematic, not a calculated spectrum.';let q;switch(id){case 'wave':return `ν = c/λ = 299 792 458 / (${p.lambda} × 10⁻⁹) = <strong>${fmt(P.C/(p.lambda*1e-9))} Hz</strong><br>E = hc/λ = <strong>${fmt(P.H*P.C/(p.lambda*1e-9)/P.EV)} eV</strong><br>I/Iref = ${fmt(p.amp)}² = <strong>${fmt(p.amp**2)}</strong>`;case 'interference':return `Δx ≈ λL/d = (${p.lambda} × 10⁻⁹ × ${fmt(p.L)}) / (${fmt(p.d)} × 10⁻³) = <strong>${fmt(p.lambda*1e-9*p.L/(p.d*1e-3)*1000)} mm</strong><br>The screen scale stays fixed at −15…+15 mm, so changes in fringe spacing remain visible without rescaling the field.${p.path?'<br>Coherence is lost: there are no fine fringes. The calculated spacing describes the coherent comparison case only.':''}`;case 'diffraction':q=P.outputs(id,p,0);return `${p.kind==='grating'?'sin θ<sub>env</sub>':'sin θ₁'} = ${p.kind==='circle'?'1,21967 × ':''}λ/a = ${p.kind==='circle'?'1,21967 × ':''}${p.lambda} × 10⁻⁹ / (${fmt(p.width)} × 10⁻⁶)<br>${p.kind==='grating'?'θ<sub>env</sub>':'θ₁'} = <strong>${fmt(q[p.kind==='grating'?'Envelope-minimum angle (deg)':'First-minimum angle (deg)'])}°</strong>${p.kind==='grating'?`<br>First grating minimum: sin θ₁ = λ/(Nd) = ${p.lambda}/(${p.n} × ${p.spacing} × 1000)<br>θ₁ = <strong>${fmt(q['First-minimum angle (deg)'])}°</strong>`:''}`;case 'polarization':q=P.polarization(p);return `Before the first filter, I = ${fmt(q.stokes[0],5)} ${p.mode==='water'?'of the light incident on the water':'of the source flux'}.<br>${q.stages.map((s,i)=>`Filter ${i+1}, axis ${s.angle}°: I<sub>${i+1}</sub> = <strong>${fmt(s.intensity,5)}</strong>`).join('<br>')}<br>For the first: I<sub>1</sub> = ½[I + Q cos(2θ) + U sin(2θ)]. For subsequent filters: I<sub>j</sub> = I<sub>j−1</sub> cos²(θ<sub>j</sub> − θ<sub>j−1</sub>).${p.mode==='water'?`<br>R<sub>s</sub> = ${fmt(q.rs,5)}; R<sub>p</sub> = ${fmt(q.rp,5)}; θ<sub>B</sub> = ${fmt(q.brewster,2)}°. Reflection and outgoing glare are given as percentages of light incident on the water. Filter transmission is a percentage of the glare before the filters. These denominators differ.`:''}`;case 'refraction':q=P.refraction(p);return p.prism?(()=>{const rows=[400,550,700].map(nm=>{const q=P.prism(nm,p.material,p.prismAngle,p.apex);return `<strong>${nm} nm</strong>: n = ${fmt(q.n,5)}<br>r<sub>1</sub> = arcsin[sin(${q.incidence}°)/${fmt(q.n,5)}] = ${fmt(q.r1)}°<br>r<sub>2</sub> = ${q.apex}° − ${fmt(q.r1)}° = ${fmt(q.r2)}°<br>${q.tir?'Total internal reflection at the second face.':`e = arcsin[n sin(r<sub>2</sub>)] = ${fmt(q.emergence)}°<br>δ = i + e − A = ${fmt(q.deviation)}°`}`});const b=P.prism(400,p.material,p.prismAngle,p.apex),r=P.prism(700,p.material,p.prismAngle,p.apex);return `White input: all colours from 400 to 700 nm.<br>i = ${b.incidence}°; A = ${b.apex}°.<br><br>${rows.join('<br><br>')}<br><br>Separation inside: |r<sub>1,400</sub> − r<sub>1,700</sub>| = <strong>${fmt(Math.abs(b.r1-r.r1))}°</strong><br>Separation of outgoing directions: |δ<sub>400</sub> − δ<sub>700</sub>| = <strong>${fmt(Math.abs(b.deviation-r.deviation))}°</strong>. A dash means that one colour does not leave through the second face. Zoom and close-up views do not change these calculations.`})():`n₁ = ${fmt(q.n1,4)}; n₂ = ${fmt(q.n2,4)}<br>sin θ₂ = (${fmt(q.n1,4)}/${fmt(q.n2,4)}) × sin(${p.angle}°)<br>${q.theta===null?'<strong>Value > 1: total internal reflection.</strong>':`θ₂ = <strong>${fmt(q.theta)}°</strong>`}${q.critical!==null?`<br>θcrit = ${fmt(q.critical)}°`:''}`;case 'photoelectric':q=P.photo(p);return `E = hc/λ = <strong>${fmt(q.e)} eV</strong>; W = ${q.w} eV<br>${q.e<q.w?'E < W: there is no single-photon photoelectric emission.':`Kmax = ${fmt(q.e)} − ${q.w} = <strong>${fmt(q.ke)} eV</strong><br>Ustop = ${fmt(q.ke)} V; U = ${fmt(p.voltage)} V`}`;case 'atom':q=P.atom(p);if(q.tabled)return `<strong>${q.species.name} (${q.species.symbol})</strong><br>Upper state: ${q.upperLabel}, E = ${fmt(q.eUpper,5)} eV<br>Lower state: ${q.lowerLabel}, E = ${fmt(q.eLower,5)} eV<br>ΔE = (${fmt(q.upperCm,4)} − ${fmt(q.lowerCm,4)}) cm⁻¹ × hc = <strong>${fmt(q.de,5)} eV</strong><br>λ<sub>vac</sub> = 10⁷ / ${fmt(q.upperCm-q.lowerCm,4)} = <strong>${fmt(q.lambda,3)} nm</strong><br>NIST: ${fmt(q.lambdaTable,5)} nm (${q.medium}).<br><a href="${P.atomSource(p.species)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NIST level and line data ↗</a>`;return `ΔE = 13,5983 × (1/${q.lower}² − 1/${q.upper}²) = <strong>${fmt(q.de)} eV</strong><br>λ = hc/ΔE = <strong>${fmt(q.lambda,2)} nm</strong>`;case 'molecule':q=P.molecule(p);return p.transition==='fluorescence'?`3,10 eV = 2.40 eV + 0.70 eV<br>λabs = 399.95 nm; λem = <strong>${fmt(q.lambda,2)} nm</strong>`:`ΔE = <strong>${fmt(q.de,6)} eV</strong><br>λ = hc/ΔE = <strong>${fmt(q.lambda,2)} nm</strong><br>The selected model line is shown among other transitions.`;case 'sky':q=P.sky(p);return `τR(550 nm) = 0.10 × fgas × ${fmt(p.pressure)} = <strong>${fmt(q.tau550)}</strong><br>Direct-light path through the shell: <strong>${fmt(q.path,1)} km</strong><br>For each λ, we apply exp(−τ), then integrate single scattering. Colour swatches are normalised in brightness.`;default:q=P.star(p);return `λmax = 2,89777 × 10⁶ / ${p.T} = <strong>${fmt(q.peak,1)} nm</strong><br>F = σ × ${p.T}⁴ = <strong>${fmt(q.flux)} W/m²</strong><br>L = 4π × (${fmt(p.radius)} × 6,957 × 10⁸)² × F = <strong>${fmt(q.lum)} W</strong>`}}
function tick(now){if(!running||!active)return;if(now-last>=32){time+=Math.min((now-last)/1000,.1);last=now;if(Number.isFinite(transitionDuration())&&time>=transitionDuration()){time=transitionDuration();running=false;}updatePhotons();render(true);if(!running){updateButtons();return}}frame=requestAnimationFrame(tick)}
function route(){clearInterval(skyTimer);skyTimer=null;if(active&&['#calculations','#main'].includes(location.hash)){$(location.hash)?.scrollIntoView();return}running=false;cancelAnimationFrame(frame);let hash=location.hash,id=hash.startsWith('#lab/')?hash.slice(5):null;let e=exps.find(q=>q.id===id);if(e){lab(e);scrollTo(0,0)}else if(!active&&main.innerHTML&&['#experiments','#basics'].includes(hash)){$(hash)?.scrollIntoView()}else{active=null;document.title='Light — INSCIENCE LAB';home();if(['#experiments','#basics'].includes(hash))requestAnimationFrame(()=>$(hash)?.scrollIntoView());else scrollTo(0,0)}}
function record(){let out=P.outputs(active.id,params,time),values={};for(let f of active.fields)if(typeof params[f.key]==='number'&&!$('#p-'+f.key).disabled&&!$('#p-'+f.key).closest('.field').hidden)values[f.label.replace(/<[^>]+>/g,'')+(f.unit?' ('+f.unit+')':'')]=params[f.key];Object.assign(values,out);records.push({id:Date.now()+'-'+Math.random().toString(16).slice(2),experiment:active.id,title:active.title,date:new Date().toISOString(),time,params:{...params},values});persist();toast('Measurement recorded. Open the notebook for the graph and CSV.')}
$('#journalOpen').onclick=()=>{fillJournal();$('#journal').showModal();requestAnimationFrame(plotJournal)};$('#journalClose').onclick=()=>$('#journal').close();$('#journal').onclick=ev=>{if(ev.target===$('#journal')){let r=$('#journal').getBoundingClientRect();if(ev.clientX<r.left||ev.clientX>r.right||ev.clientY<r.top||ev.clientY>r.bottom)$('#journal').close()}};$('#clear').onclick=()=>{if(!records.length)return;if(confirm('Delete all records from this browser? Save the CSV first if you need a copy.')){records=[];persist();fillJournal();plotJournal()}};
function fillJournal(){let selected=$('#plotExp').value;let options=exps.filter(e=>records.some(r=>r.experiment===e.id));$('#plotExp').innerHTML=options.length?options.map(e=>`<option value="${e.id}">${e.title}</option>`).join(''):'<option value="">No measurements</option>';if(options.some(e=>e.id===selected))$('#plotExp').value=selected;else if(active&&options.some(e=>e.id===active.id))$('#plotExp').value=active.id;fillAxes();$('#rows').innerHTML=records.length?`<table><thead><tr><th>№</th><th>Experiment</th><th>Animation time, s (if applicable)</th><th>Result</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody>${records.map((r,i)=>`<tr><td>${i+1}</td><td>${esc(r.title)}</td><td>${animatedIds.includes(r.experiment)?number(r.time):'—'}</td><td>${Object.entries(r.values).slice(-3).map(([k,v])=>`${mathMarkup(esc(k))}: ${number(v)}`).join('; ')}</td><td><button data-remove="${r.id}" aria-label="Delete measurement ${i+1}">×</button></td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table>`:'<p>No measurements yet. Open an experiment and click “Record measurement”.</p>';$('#rows').onclick=ev=>{let id=ev.target.closest('[data-remove]')?.dataset.remove;if(id){records=records.filter(r=>r.id!==id);persist();fillJournal();plotJournal()}}}
function plainLabel(k){return k.replaceAll('I/Iin','(fraction of initial intensity)').replaceAll('Kmax','Maximum kinetic energy').replaceAll('Bλ','Spectral radiance').replaceAll('R☉','solar radii').replaceAll('L☉','solar luminosities').replace(/<[^>]*>/g,'')}
function fillAxes(){let relevant=records.filter(r=>r.experiment===$('#plotExp').value),keys=[...new Set(relevant.flatMap(r=>Object.keys(r.values)))];for(let s of ['#plotX','#plotY'])$(s).innerHTML=keys.map(k=>`<option value="${esc(k)}">${esc(plainLabel(k))}</option>`).join('');if(keys.length>1)$('#plotY').selectedIndex=keys.length-1;}
let journalData={pts:[]};function plotJournal(hover=null){let x=$('#plotX').value,y=$('#plotY').value;let pts=records.filter(r=>r.experiment===$('#plotExp').value).map(r=>[r.values[x],r.values[y]]).filter(q=>q.every(Number.isFinite)).sort((a,b)=>a[0]-b[0]);journalData={pts,xlabel:x,ylabel:y,scatter:true};let nearest=drawChart($('#journalPlot'),journalData,hover);if(nearest)$('#plotRead').textContent=`${x}: ${number(nearest[0])} · ${y}: ${number(nearest[1])}`}
$('#plotExp').onchange=()=>{fillAxes();plotJournal()};$('#plotX').onchange=$('#plotY').onchange=()=>plotJournal();$('#journalPlot').addEventListener('pointermove',ev=>plotJournal(ev.clientX-ev.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect().left));$('#csv').onclick=()=>{if(!records.length){toast('Record a measurement in an experiment first.');return}let headers=['number','date_ISO','experiment','animation_time_s','parameter_or_result','value','settings_JSON'],rows=[headers];records.forEach((r,i)=>Object.entries(r.values).forEach(([k,v])=>rows.push([i+1,r.date,r.title,animatedIds.includes(r.experiment)?r.time:'',k,Number.isFinite(v)?v:'',JSON.stringify(r.params)])));let csv='\ufeff'+rows.map(row=>row.map((v,j)=>'"'+String(typeof v==='string'&&window.lightExportText&&(row===headers||j===2||j===4)?window.lightExportText(v):v).replaceAll('"','""')+'"').join(';')).join('\r\n');let url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([csv],{type:'text/csv;charset=utf-8'})),a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='INSCIENCE-Svitlo-'+new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10)+'.csv';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);toast('CSV prepared. One measurement contains several result rows.')};
addEventListener('hashchange',route);addEventListener('resize',()=>{if(active)render();if($('#journal').open)plotJournal()});document.addEventListener('visibilitychange',()=>{if(document.hidden&&running){running=false;cancelAnimationFrame(frame);updateButtons()}});persist();route();

function bindPrismViewport(){
 const canvas=$('#scene');let drag=null;
 const save=()=>{try{sessionStorage.setItem('light-params-refraction',JSON.stringify(params))}catch{}};
 const draw=()=>{render();save()};
 canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown',ev=>{if(!params.prism||ev.button!==0||drag)return;ev.preventDefault();canvas.focus({preventScroll:true});canvas.setPointerCapture(ev.pointerId);drag={id:ev.pointerId,x:ev.clientX,y:ev.clientY,px:params.panX||0,py:params.panY||0};canvas.classList.add('dragging')});
 canvas.addEventListener('pointermove',ev=>{if(!drag||ev.pointerId!==drag.id)return;const b=canvas.getBoundingClientRect();params.panX=drag.px+(ev.clientX-drag.x)/b.width;params.panY=drag.py+(ev.clientY-drag.y)/b.height;render()});
 const end=ev=>{if(!drag||ev.pointerId!==drag.id)return;drag=null;canvas.classList.remove('dragging');save()};
 canvas.addEventListener('pointerup',end);canvas.addEventListener('pointercancel',end);canvas.addEventListener('lostpointercapture',end);
 canvas.addEventListener('keydown',ev=>{if(!params.prism)return;const d={ArrowLeft:[-.05,0],ArrowRight:[.05,0],ArrowUp:[0,-.05],ArrowDown:[0,.05]}[ev.key];if(d){ev.preventDefault();params.panX=(params.panX||0)+d[0];params.panY=(params.panY||0)+d[1];draw()}else if(ev.key==='Home'){ev.preventDefault();$('#prismHome').click()}});
 $('#prismHome').onclick=()=>{params.panX=0;params.panY=0;params.prismZoom=1;params.prismView='overview';$('#p-prismZoom').value=1;$('#o-prismZoom').textContent='1 ×';$('#p-prismView').value='overview';draw()};
}
